.SH NAME
copyright \- the text a package shows when it is installed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B install/copyright
.SH DESCRIPTION
A package may carry a
.B copyright
file, named in its prototype(5) as
.BR "i copyright" .
It is plain text, any number of lines, and holds the package's
copyright and licence notice.
.PP
.BR pkgadd (1M)
prints it, unchanged, near the start of the installation, before any file
is installed.  A package without the file prints its
.B VENDOR
parameter from
.BR pkginfo (5)
instead, when it has one.
.BR apkg (1)
passes pkgadd's output through, so the text appears there too.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
Copyright (c) 2026 Example Author.
Distributed under the MIT license; see /opt/amix/share/doc/example.
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkginfo (5),
.BR prototype (5),
.BR pkgadd (1M)
